  "response": "\nTo calculate the area of a triangle, we can use the formula:\n\nArea = (base \u00d7 height) / 2\n\nIn this case, the base of the triangle is 3 cm + 4 cm + 5 cm = 12 cm, and the height is 6 cm.\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is:\n\nArea = (12 cm \u00d7 6 cm) / 2 = 72 cm^2\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is 72 cm^2.",
